# Auto-push to GitHub

When the user's requested work is done, commit the relevant files and push `main` to `origin` without waiting to be asked.

- Follow the existing git safety rules (no force push, no config changes, no skipped hooks).
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials).
- Write a short commit message that explains why.
- Then `git push -u origin HEAD`.
- If there is nothing to commit, still push if the branch is ahead of origin.
